functor: 1
title: script
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`script` · style · a family, a category or a transform.

# Form

`x.script` on a symbol, `(a + b).script` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `L.script` | $L.script$ | font letter |
| `F.script` | $F.script$ | font letter |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A family, a category or a transform. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | For a kind of object, prefer `object` and a `set` rule. Use the operation for fixed notation, such as `R.bb`. |
| Construction | Another alphabet for a letter: bold, double-struck, fraktur, script, upright. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.
- Works on a single letter, as the first operation.

# From LaTeX

`\mathcal{L}` and `\mathscr{L}` become `L.script`.

